## Prerequisites

- A C++{{ cpp_standard | regex_replace(pat="C\\+\\+", repl="") }} compatible compiler ({{ compiler }})
- GNU Make or compatible make utility

## Building

### Quick Start

Build the project:
```bash
make
```

This will:
1. Create necessary directories (`build/`, `bin/`)
2. Compile source files
3. Link the final target

### Build Targets

- `make` or `make all` - Build the project
- `make clean` - Remove build artifacts
- `make rebuild` - Clean and build
- `make run` - Build and run (executables only)
- `make install` - Install to system (/usr/local)
{% if include_tests %}
- `make test` - Build and run tests
- `make run-tests` - Run tests (if already built)
{% endif %}
- `make help` - Show available targets
- `make debug` - Show build configuration

### Running

{% if project_type == "executable" %}After building, run the executable:
```bash
make run
# or directly:
./bin/{{ project_name | snake_case }}
```{% else %}This is a library project. After building:
```bash
make install  # Install to system
```

Then link against it in other projects:
```bash
g++ your_app.cpp -L/usr/local/lib -l{{ project_name | snake_case }} -I/usr/local/include
```{% endif %}

## Testing

{% if include_tests %}
This project includes simple assert-based tests.

### Running Tests

Build and run tests:
```bash
make test
```

Or run tests separately:
```bash
make test
./bin/tests
```

### Test Structure

- Test files are in `tests/`
- Uses C++ `assert` for simple test cases
- Tests are compiled separately from the main project
{% else %}
Testing is not enabled for this project. To enable testing, regenerate the project with `include_tests=true`.
{% endif %}

## Build Configuration

You can modify build settings in the Makefile:

- `CPP_STANDARD`: C++ standard (default: {{ cpp_standard | regex_replace(pat="C\\+\\+", repl="") }})
- `BUILD_TYPE`: Debug or Release (default: {{ build_type }})
- `COMPILER`: C++ compiler (default: {{ compiler }})

Example debug build:
```bash
make BUILD_TYPE=Debug
```

## Project Structure

```
{{ project_name | snake_case }}/
├── Makefile               # Build configuration
├── README.md              # This file
├── .gitignore             # Git ignore patterns
├── src/                   # Source files
│   ├── {% if project_type == "executable" %}main.cpp{% else %}{{ project_name | snake_case }}.cpp{% endif %}
│   └── {{ project_name | snake_case }}.cpp
├── include/               # Header files
│   └── {{ project_name | snake_case }}.hpp
{% if include_tests %}├── tests/                 # Test files
│   └── test_main.cpp
{% endif %}
├── build/                 # Object files (generated)
└── bin/                   # Executables/libraries (generated)
```

## Manual Compilation

If you prefer not to use the Makefile:

{% if project_type == "executable" %}
```bash
mkdir -p bin
{{ compiler }} -std=c++{{ cpp_standard | regex_replace(pat="C\\+\\+", repl="") }} -Wall -Wextra -Iinclude src/main.cpp -o bin/{{ project_name | snake_case }}
```
{% else %}
```bash
mkdir -p build bin
{{ compiler }} -std=c++{{ cpp_standard | regex_replace(pat="C\\+\\+", repl="") }} -Wall -Wextra -Iinclude -c src/{{ project_name | snake_case }}.cpp -o build/{{ project_name | snake_case }}.o
{% if project_type == "static-lib" %}
ar rcs bin/lib{{ project_name | snake_case }}.a build/{{ project_name | snake_case }}.o
{% else %}
{{ compiler }} -shared build/{{ project_name | snake_case }}.o -o bin/lib{{ project_name | snake_case }}.so
{% endif %}
```
{% endif %}

